>I think that a really convenient feature to introduce
>in Nethack would be the ability to record and review
>personal notes about the game in progress.
>
>You could also use this feature to remember the musical
>notes for the drawbridge when they are given to you by
>your god, to remember important rooms ("chaotic altar
>on level 7") and important items left behind, and to
>record any information you find out about yourself or
>other creatures (through a potion of enlightenment or
>wand of probing).
>
>I'm not sure of the exact mechanics, but it could be
>something like an extended command ("#gamenotes" ?),
>which would show you the game notes, and allow you to
>add or delete notes.

The idea is excellent.  I would be using that feature
a lot.

In fact I always have a piece of paper and a pen to take
notes when I play.  So the # gamenotes would be extremely
useful.
